    <string name="cursor_assistant_title">Cursor assistant</string>
    <string name="cursor_assistant_info">In a text field, double-tap the keyboard touchpad to enter text cursor mode. Swipe to move the cursor up, down, left or right. Double-tap again, or just start typing, to leave it.</string>
    <string name="slide_light_title">Slide to turn on the keyboard light</string>
    <string name="slide_light_summary">When the keyboard light is off, a long sideways swipe across the keys turns it back on</string>
    <string name="slide_light_summary_off">Not available while the backlight is set to Always off</string>
    <string name="alt_wake_title">Alt key wake keyboard</string>
    <string name="alt_wake_summary">Press Alt to turn the screen on while it is off</string>
    <string name="scroll_assistant_info">Swipe across the keyboard to scroll the screen in apps that scroll up and down or sideways.</string>
    <string name="scroll_assistant_help">\nIf scrolling feels wrong in an app, pick a different mode for it.</string>
    <string name="scroll_assistant_summary">Slide and click: swipe to scroll, tap to click.\nSliding Mode 1: swipe to scroll, taps are ignored.\nSliding Mode 2: acts like a mouse wheel, only in apps that support one.\nMouse Mode 1: the left two fifths of the touchpad move a mouse pointer; the rest scrolls, and a tap there clicks at the pointer.\nMouse Mode 2: the same, with the right two fifths moving the pointer.</string>
