    <string name="footer_sym">Opens the symbol picker of the keyboard app, if it has one.</string>
    <string name="footer_media">Press once to play or pause, twice for the next track, hold for the previous track.</string>
    <string name="footer_magic">Hold this key and press a letter to run that letter\'s shortcut, in any app.</string>
    <string name="footer_shift">Press Shift, then a letter, for one capital. Press Shift twice to lock capitals (in Plektra).</string>
    <string name="footer_alt">Press Alt, then a key, for its Alt character. Press Alt twice to lock the Alt layer (in Plektra).</string>
    <string name="footer_power">Works like the power button: turns the screen off and on.</string>
    <string name="footer_none">%1$s does nothing now. You can make it act as another key, such as Sym or Media.</string>
    <string name="footer_shortcut">A short press, a long press and a double press can each run a function or open an app.</string>
    <string name="footer_plektra">Plektra handles Sym and Fn by scan code inside text fields, so there a remapped Sym or Fn still works as Sym or Ctrl. In Shortcut mode, and as None or Magic key, the key is taken away from the keyboard app too.</string>
